The ECP integrals -- src/core/trc_ecp_quadrature.F90, src/eri/trc_ecp_angular.F90,
src/eri/trc_ecp_radial.F90 and src/eri/trc_ecp.F90 -- are a Fortran translation of
libfint's src/cint_ecp_num.f90, cint_ecp_ang.f90, cint_ecp_rad.f90, cint_ecp.f90
and cint_ecp_drv.f90, themselves a translation of PySCF's pyscf/lib/gto/nr_ecp.c
(libcint proper has no ECP code, so this is the one part of terco's one-electron
path whose upstream is PySCF rather than libcint). Both libfint and PySCF are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; that licence applies to this
translation, under the otherwise-MIT terco tree, which is why it is named here
rather than assumed. Each file above carries its own one-line provenance header.

Basis set data
basis_sets/*.json are the Basis Set Exchange's JSON exports, unmodified
(basis_set_exchange 0.12, https://www.basissetexchange.org,
https://github.com/MolSSI-BSE/basis_set_exchange; tools/fetch_basis.py).
The data are the published basis sets of their original authors, whose papers
each file lists; see basis_sets/README.md for how to cite them and the BSE.
